  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "TRANSPOSE converts blank cells to 0 and returns #VALUE! when its input is an out-of-range @ implicit intersection",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, TRANSPOSE turns blank cells in a reference into 0 (as array formulas over blank cells do), and returns #VALUE! when given an implicit-intersection (@) reference or array-lifted @ expression whose intersection fails (e.g. ROWS(TRANSPOSE(@Data!A1:A3)) is #VALUE!, whereas ROWS(TRANSPOSE({1,2,3}*1)) is 3).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in dch9u_functions (rows 1153-1162) and matched across 1,277/1,277 full-bank TRANSPOSE rows.",
